question, from Vint Cerf.

00:13:20.573 --> 00:13:22.141
That was amazing.

00:13:22.141 --> 00:13:24.140
MELANIE WARRICK: Your
life has been perfect now.

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:25.505
You have nothing else
you need to achieve.

00:13:25.505 --> 00:13:25.760
GREG WILSON: Yeah.

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:26.580
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:28.163
Vint Cerf thinks I
ask good questions.

00:13:28.163 --> 00:13:29.180
So yeah, totally.

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:30.890
If you aren't
familiar with Vint,

00:13:30.890 --> 00:13:33.110
he's one of the founders of
the internet-- basically,

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:34.940
the thing that
allows us to do this.

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:37.400
And still, my favorite
response of all time from him

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:40.940
is when asking him, hey,
you're building this brand new,

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:42.476
distributed network,
at the time,

00:13:42.476 --> 00:13:43.850
did you think that
you were going

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:45.720
to change the world with
whatever this thing was

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:46.680
and how it was
going to come about?

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.210
And he was just like,
oh, yeah, totally.

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:49.380
FRANCESC CAMPOY FLORES: Yeah.

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:50.230
MARK MANDEL: Yeah, absolutely.

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:51.170
He was very aware of that.

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:52.280
MELANIE WARRICK: How
did you guys get him?

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:55.450
FRANCESC CAMPOY FLORES: I sent
him an email, going like, hey,

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:59.700
Vint Cerf, so we met a long
time ago at a cafe at Google.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:01.810
This is a selfie
of the two of us.

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:05.050
And so I thought that we're
doing the "Google Cloud

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:05.970
Platform Podcast."

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:07.850
Without the internet
that you invented,

00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:10.110
Google would not exists,
the Cloud would not exist,

00:14:10.110 --> 00:14:12.401
and podcasts would not exist,
so it kind of makes sense

00:14:12.401 --> 00:14:14.015
that you're the guest
for episode 100.

00:14:14.015 --> 00:14:14.765
What do you think?

00:14:14.765 --> 00:14:15.915
And he was like, OK.

00:14:15.915 --> 00:14:16.390
MELANIE WARRICK: Nice.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:17.723
FRANCESC CAMPOY FLORES: So yeah.

00:14:17.723 --> 00:14:19.010
I was like, amazing.

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:20.610
MELANIE WARRICK: Who knew how
valuable a selfie would be?

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:21.220
FRANCESC CAMPOY
FLORES: Oh, yeah.

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:21.710
GREG WILSON: Keep all selfies.

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:23.850
FRANCESC CAMPOY FLORES: You
should always take selfies.

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:25.260
MELANIE WARRICK:
Keep all the selfies.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.120
So what did you like
most about the episode,

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:30.030
outside of the fact that you
were both extremely excited

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:32.490
and you have these great
videos of you watching it?

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:33.750
FRANCESC CAMPOY FLORES: I think
that the most amazing thing was

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:35.640
that we were asking
questions about what

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:39.682
we thought the future was
and he was mentioning--

00:14:39.682 --> 00:14:41.640
for instance, we were
talking about like, well,

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:43.700
have you thought
about, in the future,

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:46.050
we'll need interplanetary
communications and things

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:46.560
like that?

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:48.430
Will TCP/IP be enough?

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:49.687
And he was like, oh, no.

00:14:49.687 --> 00:14:51.520
No, it will not because
the ping is too big.

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:53.850
But we already solved
this with the JPL protocol

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:55.730
that we invented while
working with NASA.

00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:57.720
I'm like, OK.

00:14:57.720 --> 00:15:01.230
The future, for us, is something
that he has already considered

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:04.140
and, mostly, solved,
which was amazing.

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:08.280
It's the power of
predicting and, actually,

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:12.090
even adapting, before anything
happens, to the future

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:12.757
is just amazing.

00:15:12.757 --> 00:15:13.881
MELANIE WARRICK: All right.

