00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:36.490
But then we also went to CRE--

00:23:36.490 --> 00:23:38.410
so Customer Reliability
Engineering--

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:40.960
which is the more public
facing or the customer

00:23:40.960 --> 00:23:44.300
facing side of the SRE culture
that we have here, at Google.

00:23:44.300 --> 00:23:45.970
So we had Luke Stone on--

00:23:45.970 --> 00:23:48.070
the director of Customer
Reliability Engineering--

00:23:48.070 --> 00:23:50.440
to talk about the CRE platform.

00:23:50.440 --> 00:23:53.370
We had William Bonnell
come from Home Depot.

00:23:53.370 --> 00:23:54.520
He's the customer side.

00:23:54.520 --> 00:23:56.380
Basically, they are
a company that uses

00:23:56.380 --> 00:23:58.240
our CRE and their experience.

00:23:58.240 --> 00:24:00.130
We got sort of
both sides of that.

00:24:00.130 --> 00:24:02.680
I, personally, found
it really interesting

00:24:02.680 --> 00:24:05.530
to learn more about how
we do Sire Reliability

00:24:05.530 --> 00:24:08.030
Engineering, what does that
actually mean for our products,

00:24:08.030 --> 00:24:10.404
when we start talking about
like service level objectives

00:24:10.404 --> 00:24:12.250
and service level agreements.

00:24:12.250 --> 00:24:16.480
And from a customer perspective,
if I'm building a product,

00:24:16.480 --> 00:24:19.230
I need to think about,
how much uptime do

00:24:19.230 --> 00:24:20.520
I have to have for this thing?

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:22.500
And does it correlate
with the uptime

00:24:22.500 --> 00:24:24.870
that I'm getting from the
products that I'm using?

00:24:24.870 --> 00:24:27.150
And how do those
things interrelate?

00:24:27.150 --> 00:24:28.830
How do I deal with
failure, knowing

00:24:28.830 --> 00:24:32.130
that failure is just something
that is always going to happen?

00:24:32.130 --> 00:24:34.371
And how do I deal with
that, and postmortems,

00:24:34.371 --> 00:24:36.870
and all the cool stuff that, I
think, comes along with that?

00:24:36.870 --> 00:24:39.453
I found that really interesting,
like an almost philosophical,

00:24:39.453 --> 00:24:40.979
technical discussion.

00:24:40.979 --> 00:24:41.895
